{"key":"apphycem-mcq-np1-010","kind":"mcq","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"A","final_answer":"Q/(6*epsilon_0)","working":"By Gauss's law, the total electric flux through any closed surface enclosing a net charge Q is Phi_total = Q / epsilon_0. A cube has 6 identical planar faces. Because the point charge +Q is located at the exact center of the cube, the configuration possesses full cubic symmetry. Consequently, the electric flux must be distributed equally across all 6 faces. Thus, the electric flux through one face is Phi_face = Phi_total / 6 = Q / (6 * epsilon_0).","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":385,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":385,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":386,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":148,"reasoningTokens":238},"totalTokens":771,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":238,"promptTokenCount":385,"candidatesTokenCount":148,"totalTokenCount":771,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":385}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":148}]},"reasoningTokens":238,"cachedInputTokens":0},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":3510,"keyed_label":"A"}
{"key":"apphycem-mcq-np1-010","kind":"mcq","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"A","final_answer":"Q/(6*epsilon_0)","working":"By Gauss's law, the total electric flux through the entire closed cubical surface is Q/epsilon_0. Since the charge is exactly at the center of the cube, symmetry gives equal flux through all six faces. Therefore the flux through one face is (1/6)(Q/epsilon_0) = Q/(6 epsilon_0).","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":438,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":54,"cacheReadTokens":384},"outputTokens":234,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":108,"reasoningTokens":126},"totalTokens":672,"raw":{"prompt_tokens":438,"completion_tokens":234,"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":384,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":54,"total_tokens":672,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":384},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":126}},"reasoningTokens":126,"cachedInputTokens":384},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":2637,"keyed_label":"A"}
{"key":"apphycem-mcq-np1-006","kind":"mcq","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"A","final_answer":"rho*R/(6*epsilon_0)","working":"Use a Gaussian sphere of radius r = R/2 concentric with the charged sphere. By spherical symmetry, E is constant on this surface. The enclosed charge is rho times the volume of the Gaussian sphere: Q_enc = rho*(4/3)*pi*(R/2)^3 = rho*pi*R^3/6. The Gaussian surface area is 4*pi*(R/2)^2 = pi*R^2. Gauss's law gives E*(pi*R^2) = (rho*pi*R^3/6)/epsilon_0, so E = rho*R/(6*epsilon_0).","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":458,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":74,"cacheReadTokens":384},"outputTokens":760,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":176,"reasoningTokens":584},"totalTokens":1218,"raw":{"prompt_tokens":458,"completion_tokens":760,"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":384,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":74,"total_tokens":1218,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":384},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":584}},"reasoningTokens":584,"cachedInputTokens":384},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":6570,"keyed_label":"A"}
